 ## Background
-Lit sphere shading was originally presented by Sloan et al. [SMGG01] for non-photorealistic rendering of polygonal models [S1][S2, unofficial]. It was adapted for illustrative volume rendering by [Style Transfer Functions for Illustrative Volume Rendering](S1, S2). The technique leverages the fact that a sphere under orthographic projection covers the complete set of unit normals on one hemisphere, making it an ideal proxy for capturing normal-dependent shading variations [S1][S2, unofficial].
